                "#                process_sbreff=True,         # this is temp\n",
                "#                b_sli=False, b_mot=True, b_hghp=True, b_temps=False,\n",
                "#                motcor_intp_meth = 3,         # since we are aplying we can just use sinc instead of sinc/trilin\n",
                "#                motcor_fromsdm = sdmlist,\n",
                "#                motcor_fromsdm_sbref = sbrefsdms,\n",
                "#                fnlist = fmrlist)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "Aditionally, we can apply (fsl-topup) distortion correct, directly from within this notebook. Though for this to work there are some caveats.\n",
                "+ Topup directly from within the notebook does not currently work on Mac M1, please set the optional parameter `print_cmd` : `True` and copy outputs to terminal manually\n",
                "+ Topup on Windows is currently being tested (if wsl & fsl are installed), for now you have two options:\n",
                "\t+ Add `'wsl -e '` as prefix. \n",
                "Set cmdpath manually in wsl style (e.g. `/mnt/c/outputpath`). \n",
                "Additionally maunally set conf_fil_dir (e.g. `/mnt/c/bv_preprocfolder/configs`) when running the topup merge, run and apply steps.\n",
                "\t+ Set `print_cmd` : `True` and manually copy paste the comments within the WSL instance (take care that the path name may expect `/mnt/c/path`)"
            ]
        },
