            "source": [
                "### Cleanup Intermediate Files\n",
                "Since, so far we are saving every intermediate file format, we should do some cleanup. Here we run a simple function parsing through the output folder searching for intermediate preprocessing steps and deleting them to free up some space."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 601,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "bv_preproc.utils.cleanup_intermediates(output_dir, [1], [2], first_preproc='slicescan', bv=bv)\n",
                "# bv_preproc.utils.cleanup_nifis(output_dir, [1], [2], bv=bv) #additional we could probably delete the nii file files for now"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "***\n",
                "# Anatomical Data Preprocessing\n",
                "We do the same for our anatomical data, first we take the prepaired dicoms, create `vmr` and `v16` files from them, and apply multiple preprocessing steps.\n",
                "### Anatomical Settings"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 1004,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "pps            = [2] # list of participant(s) to parse through (or single value)\n",
                "sess_anat           = [1] # list of session(s) to parse through (or single value) for ananatomical\n",
                "\n",
                "mp2rage_factor        = 6 # denoising factor for mp2rage noise\n",
                "erosion_itter         = 4 # number of errosion itterations\n",
                "erosion_mask_int      = 0.6 # intensity of erosion mask\n",
                "\n",
                "isovoxel_framing_cube = 512 # the framing cube to use for isovoxeled data \n",
                "isovoxel_res          = 0.4 # target resolution\n",
                "isovoxel_intp         = 2 # interpolation method for isovoxel (1:trilinear, 2:cubic spline, 3:sinc interpolation)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### Create Anatomical \n",
                "First we create the necessary files using `create_vmr` or `create_vmrs`, note that these function rely on keywords obtained from the raw dicom files (which need to be be prepaired using the steps outlined in `Prepair Dicoms`). Possible keywords can be T1, Mp2rage etc., though these are not exclusive and should be added to the `anatomical_dir_information` function for feature formats (or alternatively, this step can be done manually be creating vmr for the needed file format)."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 847,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "bv_preproc.anatomical.create_vmrs(bv, input_dir, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, key='KeysMp2rage')\n",
                "bv_preproc.anatomical.create_vmrs(bv, input_dir, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, key='KeysT1')\n",
                "bv_preproc.anatomical.create_vmrs(bv, input_dir, output_dir, pps, sess, key='KeysAngulated') # in some cases we have anatomical data from several sessions"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### Denoise MP2Rage Data\n",
                "Please note that here we make an example for 1 participant, cases looping over multiple participants will be slightly different"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 848,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "Denoising MP2Rage, using: UNI.v16, INV1.v16, and INV2.v16, output file: uniden.v16\n",
                        "V16 saved.\n",
                        "VMR saved."
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "header, uniden = bv_preproc.anatomical.mp2rage_genuniden(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), mp2rage_factor) \n",
                "\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "## [CASE: MULTIPLE PARTICIPANTS] ##\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "#bv_preproc.anatomical.mp2rage_genuniden_all(output_dir, pps, sess_anat, mp2rage_factor, bv=bv)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "Plotting to see if the MP2Rage went OK"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 849,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": ""
                    },
                    "name": "image-1",
                    "output_type": "display_data"
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "ax, fig = bv_preproc.anatomical_plot.plot_mp2rage_denois(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), bv=bv)\n",
                "nbt.embed(fig)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### Anatomical Preprocessing\n",
                "Next we do other preprocessing steps to cleanup our anatomical data. First we correct inhomogenities in the data, next we optimize our brainmask (in the hoops to get rid of most of the peal surface for better corregistration). Last we isovoxel both the brainvoyager masked uniden image and the optimized mask image.\n",
                "These steps should prepair the anatomicals to be used with the coregistration step.\n",
                "#### 1. Inhomogenity correction\n",
                "The inhomogenty correction step will remove inhomogenties in the image caused by (amongst others) air/tissue interfaces. The underlying BrainVoyager function will also create a (somewhat rough) deskulling mask, this we use in step 2b if we decide to take this path."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 850,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical.correct_inhomogeneities(bv, join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])))\n",
                "\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "## [CASE: MULTIPLE PARTICIPANTS] ##\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "#bv_preproc.anatomical.correct_inhomogeneities_all(bv, output_dir, pps, sess_anat)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "#### 2a. BrainMask optimization\n",
                "Next we create a brainmask to filter away both skull and dura. For this step I present two options, the first (and better) option uses nighres to estimate dura matter directly for the second inversion image.\n",
                "It will then use this estimation to create an new alpha mask to remove dura from the brainmask.\n",
                "Note that this option does require access to `nighres` (see https://nighres.readthedocs.io/en/latest/installation.html for more information). To have these functions working fully within BrainVoyager notebooks, Linux is required. Though nighres can be run in both Mac and Windows using Docker. Just run the `bv_preproc.anatomical_nighres.create_removedura_mask` and `bv_preproc.anatomical_nighres.apply_removedura_mask` inside the Docker notebook instead."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 851,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "MP2RAGE Skull Stripping\n",
                        "\n",
                        "MP2RAGE Dura Estimation\n",
                        "VMR saved.\n",
                        "V16 saved."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": ""
                    },
                    "name": "image-1",
                    "output_type": "display_data"
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "# import brainvoyager nighres functions\n",
                "import bv_preproc.anatomical_nighres\n",
                "\n",
                "# create mask apha file and apply\n",
                "duramask = bv_preproc.anatomical_nighres.create_removedura_mask(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), t1_fn='T1.v16', bv=bv)\n",
                "doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical_nighres.apply_removedura_mask(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), duramask, bv=bv)\n",
                "\n",
                "# and plot to see if everything worked as intended\n",
                "ax, fig = bv_preproc.anatomical_plot.plot_removedura_mask(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), duramask, 'UNI.vmr', bv=bv)\n",
                "nbt.embed(fig)\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "## [CASE: MULTIPLE PARTICIPANTS] ##\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "#bv_preproc.anatomical_nighres.removedura_all(output_dir, pps, sess_anat, t1_fn='T1.v16', bv=bv)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### 2b. BrainMask optimization (by eroding bv mask)\n",
                "Alternatively we could just take the mask brain BrainVoyager created for us and erode it (note that we only need to leave the white matter intact, so we can erode quite a bit before running into problems).\n",
                "This function is quite a bit faster compared to 2a, and works on Windows / Mac without any tinkering. Though it may require some playing around with the number of errosion steps."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": -1,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "bv_preproc.anatomical.erode_mask(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), itterations=erosion_itter, bv=bv)\n",
                "doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical.apply_erosion_mask(join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), outmask_int=erosion_mask_int, bv=bv)\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "## [CASE: MULTIPLE PARTICIPANTS] ##\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "#bv_preproc.anatomical.erode_mask_all(output_dir, pps, sess_anat, itterations=erosion_itter, bv=bv)\n",
                "#bv_preproc.anatomical.apply_erosion_mask_all(output_dir, pps, sess_anat, outmask_int=erosion_mask_int, bv=bv)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "#### 3. Isovoxel so that coregistration can happen\n",
                "Lastly, we isovoxel to a value where anatomical and functional data are understood by BrainVoyagers coregistration functions (they must be able to allign).\n",
                "We isovoxel both the automatically masked (with Dura intact) and the new masked uniden images, this way after calculating coregistration, during aplication we can use the 'more raw' file."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 852,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical.isovoxel(bv, join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), 'uniden_IIHC_masked', \n",
                "                                         res=isovoxel_res, \n",
                "                                         interpolation=isovoxel_intp,\n",
                "                                         framing_cube=isovoxel_framing_cube)\n",
                "doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical.isovoxel(bv, join(output_dir, prefix(pps[0],sess_anat[0])), 'uniden_IIHC',  \n",
                "                                         res=isovoxel_res, \n",
                "                                         interpolation=isovoxel_intp,\n",
                "                                         framing_cube=isovoxel_framing_cube)\n",
                "    \n",
                "                                     \n",
                "###################################\n",
                "## [CASE: MULTIPLE PARTICIPANTS] ##\n",
                "###################################\n",
                "#doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical.isovoxel_all(bv, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, 'uniden_IIHC_masked', \n",
                "#                                         res=isovoxel_res, \n",
                "#                                         interpolation=isovoxel_intp,\n",
                "#                                         framing_cube=isovoxel_framing_cube)\n",
                "#doc_vmr = bv_preproc.anatomical.isovoxel_all(bv, joutput_dir, pps, sess_anat, 'uniden_IIHC',  \n",
                "#                                         res=isovoxel_res, \n",
                "#                                         interpolation=isovoxel_intp,\n",
                "#                                         framing_cube=isovoxel_framing_cube)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "***\n",
                "# Coregistration\n",
                "Using the prepaired anatomical data we can now coregister. First we do an initial coregistration from the sbref(can use another volume) to the 'uniden_IIHC_masked' image. \n",
                "This initial coregistration will create a boundary map we can apply for all our runs, this time to the uneroded 'uniden_IIHC'.\n",
                "### Coregister Settings"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 996,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "# vmr filenames\n",
                "vmr_masked_fn = 'uniden_IIHC_masked_ISO-0.4.vmr'\n",
                "vmr_fn = 'uniden_IIHC_ISO-0.4.vmr'\n",
                "\n",
                "# take the fmr filename - here we use the sbref\n",
                "fmr_fn = 'run1_SBRef_FMR_3DMCTS_TOPUP.fmr'"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### Coregister Step\n",
                "The Coregister step first coregister a fmr volume (I like to use sbref but other volumes should work fine as well) to our masked fmr image. \n",
                "The way BrainVoyager handles coregistration using boundary based registration is to first check if there exists an white matter mesh file, if this file doesn't exits it will create one.\n",
                "What we do here is create the white matter mesh file (srf) using the masked vmr, this way we ensure no hickups caused by the dura peal.\n",
                "\n",
                "Next we can copy this mesh file, and do the coregistration again on our not masked file. This works because BrainVoyager finds an existing mesh file and goes straight to registration."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 914,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "bv_preproc.coregister.coregister_bbr_all(bv, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, vmr_masked_fn, fmr_fn)\n",
                "bv_preproc.coregister.copy_mesh_all(bv, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, vmr_masked_fn)\n",
                "bv_preproc.coregister.coregister_bbr_all(bv, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, vmr_fn, fmr_fn)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "#### (Optionally) Coregister to other session\n",
                "We could also coregister files to functional data that was measured in a different session all together (still using the saved mesh files). \n",
                "Here I coregister the run1 sbref from session 2 to the vmr of session 1."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 991,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "DocPyBV (DocPyBV at: 0xc613f70)"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "fmr_fn_new = bv_preproc.coregister._fmr_fn(join(output_dir, prefix(1,2)), fmr_fn)\n",
                "bv_preproc.coregister.coregister_bbr(bv, join(output_dir, prefix(1,1)), vmr_fn, fmr_fn_new, fmr_dir=join(output_dir, prefix(1,2)))"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "#### Plotting & Senity checks\n",
                "Plotting and senity checks for coregistration currently fully rely on the bv.embed_viewer option (which is slow). However, BrainVoyager will open the coregistration results in the image window. \n",
                "Look here wether allignment is oke by use the `f8` & `f9` keys on the keyboard."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 1200,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": ""
                    },
                    "name": "image-1",
                    "output_type": "display_data"
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "coreg_doc = bv.active_document\n",
                "coreg_doc.embed_viewer()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "***\n",
                "# VTC Creation\n",
                "The next, and last preprocessing step is to take our coregistered fmr volumes and create vtc files (voxel time course files), basically creating files that we can then easily use for analyses.\n",
                "The implementation I use creates bounding boxes based on our first volume (so that we are somewhat limiting the data we have to save). \n",
                "This bounding box is then used to create the actual vtc files (x from/to, y from/to, z from/to). The actual vtc files will have a resolution of to minus from in 3 dimensions * number of volumes.\n",
                "### Settings"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 1011,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "# sellect list of fmr's and vmr file of interest\n",
                "fmr_list = bv_preproc.utils.preproc_filenames(join(output_dir, prefix(2, 1)), sbref=2, slicor=True,motcor=True,hpfil=True,tpsmo=False,topup=True)\n",
                "vmr_fn = 'uniden_IIHC_ISO-0.4.vmr'\n",
                "\n",
                "# sellect trf files\n",
                "ia_trf_fn = bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.ia_fn(join(output_dir, prefix(2, 1)))[0]\n",
                "fa_trf_fn = bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.fa_fn(join(output_dir, prefix(2, 1)))[0]\n",
                "#acpc_trf_fn = bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.acpc_fn(target_folder)[0]"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### VTC Creation of all runs\n",
                "We can now create vtc's off all runs within a session. When options for `vtc_list`, `ia_trf_fn`, `fa_trf_fn`, & `acpc_trf_fn` are left at `True` (default), the corresponding files are automatically obtained from the sellected directory."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 939,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "Traceback (most recent call last):\n",
                        "  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n",
                        "  File \"/media/jorvhar/Data/OneDrive_Mint/Documenten/Matlab and Python short scripts/bv_preproc/voxeltimecourse.py\", line 140, in create_vtc_bulk\n",
                        "    # get bounding box values from vtc header\n",
                        "NameError: name 'bvbabel' is not defined"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.create_vtc_bulk(bv, join(output_dir, prefix(2,1)), vmr_fn, fmr_list, vtcspace=1)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### Read Bounding Box Dimensions\n",
                "We can also read bounding box start and end positions from any vtc file."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 1015,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "vtc_fn = bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.vtc_names(fmr_list)[0]\n",
                "bounding_box_array = bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.bounding_box(join(output_dir, prefix(2,1), vtc_fn), bv=bv)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### VTC Creation across sessions\n",
                "And create `vtc` files arross sessions (here using the bounding box from the other measuring session)."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 1016,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "array([[ 39, 467],\n",
                        "       [ 71, 509],\n",
                        "       [167, 273]])"
                    ]
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "# create list of fmrs within some folder\n",
                "fmr_dir = join(output_dir, prefix(1, 2))\n",
                "fmr_list = bv_preproc.utils.preproc_filenames(fmr_dir, sbref=2, slicor=True,motcor=True,hpfil=True,tpsmo=False,topup=True)\n",
                "\n",
                "# create vtc of fmrs in different location)\n",
                "bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.create_vtc_bulk(bv, join(output_dir, prefix(1, 1)), vmr_fn, fmr_list, \n",
                "                                           first_vol_bounding_box = False,\n",
                "                                           bounding_box_array = bounding_box_array,\n",
                "                                           vtcspace=1, fmr_dir=fmr_dir, trf_dir=fmr_dir)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "#### (Alternativelly) VTC Creation looping over participants and sessions\n",
                "Alternatively we could use the high level function `create_vtc_bulk_all` to loop over participants and sessions and do vtc creation for all.\n",
                "Please note that one must be carefull with options within this function, it is for example highly advised to leave 'first_vol_bounding_box = True' to have consistence within an session.\n",
                "Within this higher level function fmr files are looked up using the `preproc_filenames` function, make sure the correct proccesing steps are sellected."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 972,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
            ],
            "source": [
                "# or loop over all participants and sessions to do automatical vtc creation\n",
                "bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse.create_vtc_bulk_all(bv, output_dir, pps, sess_anat, vmr_fn, vtcspace=1,\n",
                "                                               fmr_slicor=True, fmr_motcor=True, fmr_hpfil=True,\n",
                "                                               fmr_tpsmo=True, fmr_topup=True)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {
            },
            "source": [
                "### VTC plotting\n",
                "As a quick senity check, lets take the mean over time and plot some slices from the vtc (might take some time since we are loading MULTIPLE gb files)."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": 1071,
            "metadata": {
            },
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "image/png": ""
                    },
                    "name": "image-1",
                    "output_type": "display_data"
                }
            ],
            "source": [
                "ax, fig = bv_preproc.voxeltimecourse_plot.plot_vtcs(join(output_dir, prefix(2,2)), tpsmo=False, bv=bv)\n",
                "nbt.embed(fig)"
            ]
        }
    ],
